      {
        "elementType": "Empty"
      }
    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy ser-vants.\n\nWhen Thou wast nailed to the Cross, Thou didst gath-er to Thy-self the choirs of Mar-tyrs who in faith im-i-tat-ed Thy Pas-sion, O Gra-cious Lord. We there-fore en-treat of Thee: Grant Thou rest__ un-to them that have passed hence to__ Thee.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nIn Thy glo-ry un-speak-a-ble when Thou com-est, strik-ing fear in all, to judge the world en-tire, be well-pleased that Thy faith-ful ser-vants, whom Thou hast tak-en forth from the earth, O Re-deem--er, might meet Thee in the clouds with__ joy.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nSince Thou art the Source of Life, Thou, O Lord, by Thy di-vine man-hood dost lead forth those in bonds: Cause Thy ser-vants de-part-ed to Thee in faith to have as their dwell-ing-place the de-light__ and e-ter-nal joy of Par-a--dise.__\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nWe turned back to earth a-gain in trans-gress-ing God’s di-vine com-mand, O Vir-gin full of grace; yet through thee are we lift-ed up from the earth to Heav-en to dwell there-in, shak-ing off__ the cor-rup-tion and de-cay of__ death.__\n\nBe-hold-ing the sea of life with a surg-ing of temp-ta-tions swell-ing up on eve-ry side, I flee un-to Thy calm ha-ven, cry-ing out: Most mer-ci-ful Friend of man, bring my life__ from cor-rup-tion up to Thee, O__ Lord.__"
    }
  }
}